     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 to 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO twice or three times daily.** This is a lower dose, for example if you're starting or titrating.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg twice daily, which may be what \"1700\" was meant to be.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, or confirm that you intend 1,700 mg three times daily. If you confirm the original dose, I'll need a note with the clinical rationale on the order."
      }
     ],
